{"title":"Career roadmap · Heritage Consultant","role":"Heritage Consultant","summary":"A Heritage Consultant researches, documents, evaluates and advises on the conservation, interpretation, management and responsible use of cultural heritage. Heritage may include historic buildings, archaeological sites, monuments, museums, archives, cultural landscapes, traditions and intangible heritage.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"History"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Good alignment, but specialist training is usually needed. A BA History graduate can enter heritage research, documentation, museum, archive and project-assistant roles; independent/senior consultancy generally requires postgraduate study and field experience."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BA in History provides a strong foundation in historical research, source analysis, chronology, cultural context and documentation. For professional heritage consultancy, it should be complemented by heritage conservation, archaeology, architecture, museum studies, archival methods, GIS and project-management skills."}]},{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA History","Heritage/Museum/Archaeology Internship","Heritage Research/Project Assistant","Heritage Consultant/Heritage Officer","Senior Heritage Consultant","Heritage Project Manager/Specialist","Heritage Practice Lead / Cultural Heritage Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build historical research, documentation, heritage and fieldwork skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise through postgraduate study and heritage/archaeology/museum projects."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead heritage assessments, conservation projects, interpretation programmes or cultural-resource studies."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Become a senior heritage specialist, consultancy lead, cultural heritage manager or independent consultant."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Historical research and source analysis"},{"text":"History courses, archives, libraries"},{"text":"3 research papers"},{"text":"Research"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Heritage identification and documentation"},{"text":"Local heritage sites/museums"},{"text":"10 documented heritage assets"},{"text":"Field skills"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Archaeology and conservation fundamentals"},{"text":"University + heritage resources"},{"text":"Heritage assessment report"},{"text":"Domain knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"GIS, mapping and digital documentation"},{"text":"GIS courses/projects"},{"text":"Heritage GIS map"},{"text":"Technical skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Heritage/museum/archaeology internship"},{"text":"Institutions and field projects"},{"text":"Internship + field report"},{"text":"Industry exposure"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Heritage management and interpretation"},{"text":"Case studies + project work"},{"text":"Heritage management plan"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialist research"},{"text":"Dissertation/fieldwork"},{"text":"Major heritage study"},{"text":"Expertise"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Consultancy portfolio"},{"text":"Real/simulated projects"},{"text":"Heritage portfolio + applications"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects to prioritise"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ancient/Medieval/Modern History"},{"text":"Indian History"},{"text":"World History"},{"text":"Cultural History"},{"text":"Art History"},{"text"